+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`:
+  - `Line.vat` now uses `net * rate` (it was `unit_price * rate`, which ignored quantity). Rule 3.
+  - `Invoice.add` raises `ValueError` for rate names not in `RATES`. Rule 3.
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: `test_reduced_rate_small_item` expected VAT 0.02 / gross 0.52. 0.50 * 0.05 = 0.025, which rule 4 (round half up) rounds to 0.03, so gross is 0.53. I changed the expected values to 0.03 / 0.53.
+- `docs/PRICING.md` is untouched.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: before, 4 failures; after the code fix, 1 failure (the test above); after the test fix, all 6 tests pass (see the final run).
+- Checked by hand that the other test expectations agree with the spec (pen 2.994 -> 2.99; mixed rates 5.16).
+
+## Needs your attention
+- The test I edited was the only one that disagreed with the spec. Someone may have written 0.02 on purpose, for example banker's rounding in the accounting system. If so, finance needs to confirm the rule, because the spec says half up.
+- Not verified: quantity is not validated (negative or non-integer values are accepted), and the spec says nothing about it.
